{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1780093781,"nonce":"w16vXkGzssNS/qTz2duPNcsXurc=","metadata":{"github-id":"UCE_lAHOK4fCvM8AAAABDy-HI86_rb-x"},"target":"56173682cc1fc650e24551ffed44201e8185306000d203b0c4fe5128ba8fdc90","message":"## Purpose\n\nFirst on-water run with the **graded sea-surface costmap** ([perception #22](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_perception/issues/22) / PR [#25](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_perception/pull/25), merged 2026-05-29). This came directly out of the #186 observation: a red buoy visible in the segmentation image that never registered on the costmap.\n\n**What changed (perception):** the costmap now accumulates *graded* per-pixel softmax log-odds (prior-shifted at `obstacle_prob_min`) instead of a hard argmax + flat hit/miss + binary LETHAL. Weak-but-persistent obstacles now bank positive evidence and mark; output is a graded cost ramp (soft `1..252` + LETHAL `254`) instead of lethal-only. All knobs are runtime-tunable.\n\n**What did NOT change:** the reflex **Collision Monitor** ([#170](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/170)) is untouched. Avoidance comes from (a) the **global planner** routing around costs and (b) the reflex monitor — the controller (`CrabbingPathFollower`) is a PID path-tracker and ignores costmap cost.\n\n## Must-verify this deployment\n\n- [ ] **The #186 fix** — aim at a dim / low-contrast buoy (the kind that showed red in the segmentation image but never marked). Confirm it now appears on the costmap (rviz), and cross-check the segmentation image still shows red there.\n- [ ] **No regression on strong obstacles** — clearly-visible buoys / docks still mark LETHAL.\n- [ ] **Graded gradient is visible** — rviz shows a soft cost ramp around uncertain areas, not just binary lethal blobs.\n- [ ] **Reflex still stops** — the Collision Monitor still halts the boat for a near obstacle (unchanged path; confirm no regression).\n- [ ] **Global route bends around marks** — with an obstacle marked, the planned global path routes around it.\n- [ ] **Recovery is reasonable** — an area that read clear water, then gets a real obstacle, re-marks within a few seconds (asymmetric clamp).\n- [ ] **No false positives from glare / reflection** — reddish water / sun glint should not mark obstacle. If it does, raise `obstacle_prob_min`.\n\n## ⚠️ Watch out for (most likely surprises)\n\n1. **Over-conservative routing — inflation × more-lethal cells.** The global costmap uses `inflation_radius: 150 m` (`cost_scaling_factor: 0.05`), so every LETHAL cell inflates a 150 m standoff bubble. Pre-#22 only strong buoys marked lethal; **now weak buoys mark too** → in a buoy field the planner may route much wider or refuse gaps. **#1 thing to watch.** Lever is config-side (`inflation_radius` / `cost_scaling_factor` in `seafloor_echoboat_project11` `nav2_params.base.yaml`), not perception.\n2. **Aggressive cost weighting.** `SmacPlannerHybrid.cost_penalty: 10.0` is high → even low-confidence *soft* costs will deflect the global route. If routes swing wide around faint stuff, raise `free_threshold` (emit less soft cost) or lower `cost_penalty` (config-side).\n3. **Sensitivity vs false positives.** `obstacle_prob_min` is the dial: lower → catches fainter buoys but more false marks; higher → conservative.\n\n## 🔧 Runtime tuning (no rebuild — tune on the water)\n\nAll on the **local_costmap** `sea_surface_layer`. **Confirm the node name on the live stack first — don't guess** (a wrong name silently sets nothing): `ros2 node list | grep -i costmap`. Then e.g.:\n```bash\n# adjust namespace/node to match `ros2 node list`\nros2 param set /bizzy/local_costmap/local_costmap sea_surface_layer.obstacle_prob_min 0.30\n```\n\n| Param | Default | Effect |\n|-------|---------|--------|\n| `obstacle_prob_min` | 0.35 | **Primary dial.** Min P(obstacle) for a pixel to count; lower = more sensitive to dim buoys (more false marks), higher = conservative |\n| `max_evidence_step` | 0.85 | Per-frame evidence cap (flicker rejection; ~2 frames to lethal at default) |\n| `lethal_threshold` | 1.0 | Log-odds at/above which a cell is LETHAL |\n| `free_threshold` | 0.0 | Log-odds at/below which a cell has no opinion; between this and lethal → soft cost ramp |\n| `clear_floor` | −2.0 | Lower clamp; how fast a cleared cell can re-mark (recovery) |\n| `obstacle_clamp` | 5.0 | Upper clamp; obstacle persistence |\n| `decay_half_life_s` | 30.0 | Unobserved-evidence half-life |\n\nConstraints (a `param set` violating these is rejected, layer keeps prior value): `clear_floor ≤ free_threshold \u003c lethal_threshold ≤ obstacle_clamp`; `obstacle_prob_min ∈ (0,1)`; `max_evidence_step \u003e 0`.\n\nNote which values worked, per conditions (lighting, sea state) — these feed the durable config defaults. Bag a representative run (segmentation + costmap + plan) for offline A/B if anything looks off.\n\n## Operators\n\n- Roland + Claude Code Agent (Claude Opus 4.8, 1M context)\n\n## Hosts in use\n\n- **gabby** — boat-side Linux / ROS host (data hub)\n- **mercat** — boat-side Windows / QINSy host (if a survey phase is reached)\n- **salmon** — operator station\n\n## Notes\n\n- **Date TBD** — set the title date when the deployment firms up.\n- Standing next-deployment scope folds in here too; cross-link items as they land.\n- Config-side tuning lives in `seafloor_echoboat_project11` (`nav2_params.base.yaml`) and the BizzyBoat overlay in this repo (`bizzyboat_project11/config/nav2_overlay.yaml`).\n\n## Logs\n\n- Per-host under `docs/logs/2026/` once scheduled (`YYYY-MM-DD_\u003chost\u003e_logs.md`).\n- [dev log](docs/logs/2026/2026-05-29_dev_logs.md)\n- [gabby log](docs/logs/2026/2026-05-29_gabby_logs.md)\n- [salmon log](docs/logs/2026/2026-05-29_salmon_logs.md)\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":4,"timestamp":1780104850,"nonce":"pQk6LeiuwQVN55ANc0/NpKAUG6k=","metadata":{"github-id":"CE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABDy-HI88AAAAGFbSzLw"},"status":2}]}